            "\n",
            "\\paragraph{Overall Comments from Teachers on ChatGPT's Rating}\n",
            "After the teachers elaborated on their thoughts on the rating of ChatGPT, we ask them to provide an overall comment on how ChatGPT is doing.\n",
            "Again, the teachers are not informed that the ratings are done by an AI model.\n",
            "In summary, teachers all consider the rating and explanations reasonable. \n",
            "They find that the attributes they do not agree with are mainly \\textit{Likability} and \\textit{Cohesiveness}.\n",
            "However, they think the two attributes are a more holistic evaluation of the story and tend to be more subjective.\n",
            "Even if they do not give the same rating, they still are able to understand the explanation of ChatGPT.\n",
            "In the end, all teachers summarize that rating stories is highly subjective, and it is normal to have disagreements.\n",
            "\n",
            "\n",
            "\n",
            "\\section{LLM Evaluation}\n",
            "\\label{app: LLMs}\n",
            "\\subsection{Details on LLMs used}\n",
            "\\label{app: Details on LLMs used}\n",
            "The T0 model we use is called T0pp, which is a variant of the T0 model and has 13B parameters.\n",
            "We will still use T0 to refer to this model.\n",
            "We load the T0 model using the \\texttt{transformers} toolkit~\\citep{wolf-etal-2020-transformers}. \n",
            "The two InstructGPT models, \\texttt{text-curie-001} and \\texttt{text-davinci-003}, are queried using the \\href{https://beta.openai.com/docs/models/gpt-3}{OpenAI API}.\n",
            "We query ChatGPT using the \\href{https://chat.openai.com/chat}{OpenAI GUI}.\n",
            "While we are aware that some online resources provide an API-like tool to query ChatGPT, we think it violates the intended use of ChatGPT so we do not adopt those online resources.\n",
            "The ChatGPT we queried is the Dec. 15 and Jan. 9 version.\n",
            "\n",
            "OpenAI does not reveal the model sizes of any of the GPT models.\n",
            "However, it is estimated that \\texttt{text-curie-001} has 13B parameters and \\texttt{text-davinci-003} has 175B parameters~\\citep{GPT3size}.\n",
            "\n",
            "\\subsection{Details on Querying the LLMs}\n",
            "\\subsubsection{Parsing the LLM outputs}\n",
            "\\label{app:Parsing the LLM outputs}\n",
            "After the T0 and InstructGPT generate the answer, which is composed of several sentences in almost all cases, we parse the generated sentence to get the model's score.\n",
            "We use some rules to parse the output, and the rule is established after manually looking into the output of the generated sequences.\n",
            "First, we remove the string \\texttt{1-5} from the output since we observe that LLM will sometimes say \"\\textit{... on a scale of 1-5 ...}\", and we remove the string \\texttt{out of 5} since LLM sometimes say it \"\\textit{give a score of $x$ out of 5}\".\n",
            "We also remove the string \\texttt{/5} since LLM sometimes uses \"$x/5$\" to express that it gives a score of $x$ out of 5.\n",
            "For rating the adversarial samples, we remove the \\texttt{title 1} and \\texttt{title 2} in the output sentences.\n",
            "Last, we use the regular expression to extract the first number in the sequence.\n",
            "We find that the above rules are sufficient to parse the output and get the rating of the LLMs.\n",
            "In a few rare cases, the LLM gives the rating with a $0.5$ incremental, meaning that it gives scores like $4.5$.\n",
            "In such cases, we do not drop the $0.5$ since in our instruction, we do not explicitly tell it the rating should be 1-incremental.\n",
            "We find the LLM results merely difference between dropping the $0.5$ and keeping the $0.5$, and the results in the paper do not drop the $0.5$.\n",
            "Again, these cases are really rare.\n",
            "\n",
            "We do not parse the output of ChatGPT using any rules since we the authors read the response and extract the score by ourselves.\n",
            "\n",
            "During the experiments, ChatGPT refuses to answer the questions about 2 stories and 3 news titles since ChatGPT find those contents to violate the \\href{https://beta.openai.com/docs/usage-policies}{OpenAI content policy}.\n",
            "We find that those samples contain discrimination to some protected groups, or contain sexual or violent descriptions.\n",
            "Hence, the results of ChatGPT are calculated without those samples.\n",
            "\n",
            "\\subsubsection{Open-Ended Story Generation}\n",
            "\\label{app: task 1 instructions}\n",
            "For T0 and the two InstructGPT models, we query the four attributes \\textbf{separately} using the queries shown as follows:\n",
            "\n",
            "\\paragraph{Grammaticality}\\mbox{}\\\\\n",
            "\\texttt{\n",
            "Please rate the story fragment\\\\\n",
            "The goal of this task is to rate story fragment.\\\\\n",
            "Note: Please take the time to fully read and understand the story fragment. We will reject submissions from workers that are clearly spamming the task.\\\\\n",
            "Story fragment:\\\\}\n",
            "\\texttt{[STORY]\\\\\n",
            "\\texttt{(End of story fragment)\\\\How grammatically correct is the text of the story fragment? (on a scale of 1-5, with 1 being the lowest)}\n",
            "}\n",
            "\n",
            "\\paragraph{Cohesiveness}\\mbox{}\\\\\n",
            "\\texttt{\n",
            "Please rate the story fragment\\\\\n",
            "The goal of this task is to rate story fragment.\\\\\n",
            "Note: Please take the time to fully read and understand the story fragment. We will reject submissions from workers that are clearly spamming the task.\\\\\n",
            "Story fragment:\\\\}\n",
            "\\texttt{[STORY]\\\\\n",
            "\\texttt{(End of story fragment)\\\\How well do the sentences in the story fragment fit together? (on a scale of 1-5, with 1 being the lowest)}\n",
            "}\n",
            "\n",
            "\\paragraph{Likability}\\mbox{}\\\\\n",
            "\\texttt{\n",
            "Please rate the story fragment\\\\\n",
            "The goal of this task is to rate story fragment.\\\\\n",
            "Note: Please take the time to fully read and understand the story fragment. We will reject submissions from workers that are clearly spamming the task.\\\\\n",
            "Story fragment:\\\\}\n",
            "\\texttt{[STORY]\\\\\n",
            "\\texttt{(End of story fragment)\\\\How enjoyable do you find the story fragment? (on a scale of 1-5, with 1 being the lowest)}\n",
            "}\n",
            "\n",
            "\\paragraph{Relevance}\\mbox{}\\\\\n",
            "\\texttt{\n",
            "Please rate the story fragment\\\\\n",
            "The goal of this task is to rate story fragment.\\\\\n",
            "Note: Please take the time to fully read and understand the story fragment. We will reject submissions from workers that are clearly spamming the task.\\\\\n",
            "Story fragment:\\\\}\n",
            "\\texttt{[STORY]\\\\\n",
            "\\texttt{(End of story fragment)\\\\Now read the PROMPT based on which the story fragment was written. \\\\ PROMPT:}\n",
            "\\texttt{[PROMPT]} \n",
            "\\texttt{\\\\(End of PROMPT) \\\\How relevant is the story fragment to the prompt? (on a scale of 1-5, with 1 being the lowest)}\n",
