            "\n",
            "The \\texttt{[STORY]} and \\texttt{[PROMPT]} are to be filled in with the story and the prompt.\n",
            "We show the newlines for better readability. \n",
            "When we query the models, we use the token \\texttt{\\textbackslash n} to represent the new line.\n",
            "\n",
            "When querying ChatGPT, we query the four attributes of the same story in one conversation; this is similar to asking the teachers to rate the same story on the same page of the Google Form.\n",
            "We use the same queries shown above to query ChatGPT and the order of queries is the same as the order shown above.\n",
            "\n",
            "\\subsubsection{Adversarial Attack Quality Evaluation}\n",
            "\\label{app: Adversarial Attack Quality Evaluation}\n",
            "When querying all the LLMs in this task, we query the \\textit{fluency} and the \\textit{meaning preserving} of the same news title independently. \n",
            "This means that each conversation with ChatGPT will only have one question, asking about the fluency or the meaning preserving of news title(s).\n",
            "All the parameters for generation are the same as the default parameters in Section~\\ref{subsection: task 1 LLM Evaluation and Human Evaluation}.\n",
            "\n",
            "The exact query we use are:\n",
            "\n",
            "\\paragraph{Fluency}\\mbox{}\\\\\n",
            "\\texttt{\n",
            "You are given a news title. Please read the news title and answer the question.\\\\News title:\\\\}\n",
            "\\texttt{[NEWS\\_TITLE]}\n",
            "\\texttt{\\\\(End of news title)\\\\Question: How natural and fluent is the text of the news title? (on a scale of 1-5, with 1 being the lowest}\n",
            "\n",
            "The \\texttt{[NEWS\\_TITLE]} will be filled in with either a benign or adversarial-attacked news title.\n",
            "\n",
            "\\paragraph{Meaning Preserving}\n",
            "\\texttt{You are given two news titles. Please read the news titles and answer the question.\\\\News title 1:\\\\}\n",
            "\\texttt{[BENIGN\\_TITLE]}\n",
            "\\texttt{\\\\(End of news title 1)\\\\News title 2:\\\\}\n",
            "\\texttt{[ADVERSARIAL\\_TITLE]}\n",
            "\\texttt{\\\\(End of news title 2)\\\\Question: Do you agree that the meaning (or semantics) of news title 1 is preserved in news title 2? (on a scale of 1-5, with 1 being the strongly disagree and 5 being strongly agree.)}\n",
            "\n",
            "The \\texttt{[BENIGN\\_TITLE]} will be filled in with the news title before the attack and the \\texttt{[ADVERSARIAL\\_TITLE]} will be filled in with the news title after an adversarial attack.\n",
